===============================================================================
SECTION 1 — BEHAVIOUR REFERENCE (no code incorporated)
===============================================================================

ColaMD
  Repository : https://github.com/marswaveai/colamd
  Commit     : 4c986a4e0920cf0598fb2a47cec2966fc5340c77
  Licence    : MIT
  Read from  : ref/ColaMD/LICENSE, ref/ColaMD/package.json

ColaMD, by marswave.ai, was consulted as a *behaviour and composition
reference* while building MDX's Markdown editor. It is credited here for that
reference.

No ColaMD source code is incorporated into MDX, and none is redistributed with
it. MDX's editor was written against Milkdown's and ProseMirror's public APIs.
This was verified rather than assumed: a six-technique comparison of ColaMD's
4,247 authored lines against the 41,906 lines of packages/mdx-editor found zero
shared runs of three or more non-trivial consecutive lines, zero shared comment
lines out of 189 tested, and zero shared distinctive identifiers, CSS class
names, plugin keys or UI strings. The small residual overlap consists of
language boilerplate and the required spellings of shared library APIs. The
methods, commands and full numbers are in the audit document cited above.

Because no ColaMD code was copied and none is redistributed, the MIT clause
requiring the copyright notice to accompany "copies or substantial portions of
the Software" is not triggered. Accordingly this entry does NOT assert a
marswave.ai copyright over any MDX file — doing so would misdescribe the work.
The reference checkout lives at ref/, which is excluded from version control
and from all distributed artifacts.


