SECTION 5 — SCOPE OF THIS FILE
===============================================================================

This file covers the npm production dependency tree: 36 direct dependencies
declared in package.json and their transitive closure of 292 installed
packages. Across that closure every licence is permissive — 243 MIT, 34 ISC,
4 BSD-3-Clause, 3 Apache-2.0, 1 BSD-2-Clause, 2 dual MIT/Apache-2.0, plus the
three individually resolved cases described above. No GPL, LGPL, AGPL, SSPL or
other strong-copyleft licence appears anywhere in the tree.

Not covered here, and outstanding before release:

  - Rust crate dependencies under src-tauri/, which have their own licences and
    require a separate inventory.
  - Development-only dependencies, which are not distributed.

The listing errs toward over-inclusion: it names packages reachable in the
production dependency graph without confirming against a built bundle which of
them survive tree-shaking.
